<title>FINLAND: ASPO TO EXPAND ITS TALLINN OIL TERMINAL.</title>
<headline>ASPO TO EXPAND ITS TALLINN OIL TERMINAL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish chemicals and electronics component group Aspoyhtyma Oy said in a statement on Monday its AS Sonmarin unit will quadruple its oil terminal capacity in Tallinn, Estonia.</p>
<p>&quot;The investment will quadruple the company's container capacity in Tallinn,&quot; Aspoyhtyma said.</p>
<p>The volume of the new oil storage facility will be 46,000 cubic metres, it said.  </p>
<p>Aspoyhtyma said the new oil storage facility will be completed early next year.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0248</p>
</text>
